WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.450
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:15.390
I'm trying to create
it so it feels like it's

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:18.960
of an ancient tradition,
that it does come from people

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:19.920
figuring things out.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:22.740
And some of their technology
is really representative

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:23.910
of their culture.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:29.572
Use of jade, use of piercings,
use of body modifications.

00:00:29.572 --> 00:00:31.000
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.050
It was an interesting
design challenge

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:41.660
because we were delving
into characters that needed

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:44.150
rebreathers when they
were above water,

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:47.570
and trying to create
that look for a series

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:50.255
of warriors that needed to
look fierce and amazing.

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:56.860
Being a warrior in that culture
is sort of an extreme thing,

00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:00.220
and the idea of changing your
appearance in a way that would

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:03.190
actually allow for you to
breathe outside the water

00:01:03.190 --> 00:01:06.130
becomes an important part
of who you are as a person,

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:10.600
and it almost marks you
for life in some ways.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:14.250
We were looking at animals that
would surround them as things

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:16.470
that they could possibly
implement as looks

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:17.760
for themselves as warriors.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:20.010
So for example, with
Attuma, the fact

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:22.470
that he's got a hammerhead
shark skull that he wears

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:25.590
as a sort of helmet or headdress
becomes something that's

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:26.670
meant to be intimidating.

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:29.628
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:33.300
The same sort of
thing with Namora,

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:38.490
where we're taking sort
of oversized lionfish fins

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:43.170
and having them become an
amazing headdress for her.

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:45.090
It became one of
the cooler visuals,

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:48.520
I think, that our team put out
there is these orcas with 15,

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:50.910
20, 30 different
Talokanil attached,

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:53.775
using the undersea animals
as essentially vehicles.

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:02.960
The idea of being underwater,
of exploring an entire culture

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:04.760
that would have developed
and grown and created

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:07.730
itself into something that
was a world power I think

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:09.980
is so much fun.

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:11.480
[NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:13.930
[CHANTING]

